      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-robustus-bred/",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras robustus is one of the biggest species of its genus. Females have been measured at up to 95 mm standard length (i.e. without caudal fin). Females become somewhat bigger than males. Both sexes develop long dorsal fin rays.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-robustus-bred/",
      "html": "<p>As far as is known, there had been no reports of successful breeding in aquaria so far; bred specimens are now available. Compared to the adult animals, the body spots of the young are still clearly larger.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/corydoras-robustus-bred/",
      "html": "<p>This catfish comes from Brazil, where it is found in the drainage of the Rio Purus.</p>"
    },
